  <section class="faq-section" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="section-label">FAQ</p>
      <h2 class="section-title" id="faq-heading">Common questions</h2>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <div class="faq-item"><details><summary>What is the onboarding process?</summary><div class="faq-body">After you request a quote, we confirm your storage volume and compliance needs, then provision dedicated cloud storage accounts in your name. You receive a signed custody agreement before any data migration begins. Onboarding typically takes two to five business days depending on plan tier.</div></details></div>
        <div class="faq-item"><details><summary>Can I upgrade my plan later?</summary><div class="faq-body">Yes. Storage tiers and feature levels can be adjusted as your needs grow. We will provision additional capacity or add compliance features and update your custody agreement accordingly. Upgrades are prorated monthly.</div></details></div>
        <div class="faq-item"><details><summary>What happens to my data if I cancel?</summary><div class="faq-body">We export your data to a format you can access directly, deliver it via secure S3 presigned URL or a physical drive at your request, and provide written confirmation of delivery. Your buckets and all access credentials are then deleted after a 30-day hold period.</div></details></div>
        <div class="faq-item"><details><summary>How are creators and photographers billed differently?</summary><div class="faq-body">Creators with large archives often use a hybrid of an active plan for current work and cold archive pricing for completed projects. This keeps monthly costs manageable as your library grows. We size the tiers together during onboarding.</div></details></div>
        <div class="faq-item"><details><summary>Do you provide a BAA for HIPAA clients automatically?</summary><div class="faq-body">Yes. Any client whose data includes Protected Health Information receives a signed Business Associate Agreement before the account is provisioned. You will not be asked to store PHI without a BAA in place.</div></details></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
